preConditionHook:
// CountIF counts bars 0..N-1 INCLUDING the current bar and the counted
// condition is a true series (EL_FEATURES `countif`, VERIFIED). The counted
// condition is on PRICES, which have real history back to the chart start, so
// no zero-filled variable mirror is needed -- the same arrangement
// SpikeWithoutPullback uses.
// A tie bar (close == open within the EL tolerance) counts for neither side.
// The counts are EL numeric variables, so they are doubles here and the
// threshold comparison is an ordinary EL relational.
bearBodies = 0.0;
bullBodies = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)lookback; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(close[i], open[i])) bearBodies += 1;
    if (el_gt(close[i], open[i])) bullBodies += 1;
}

//
// AMENDED 2026-09-22 (Grimes A list, HiddenComplexPullbackBodyCount): the new
// minOpposite input turns the cap into a BAND. Long: between minOpposite and
// maxOpposite of the last lookback bars closed below their own open -- Grimes's
// "hidden" complex pullback, where one or two with-trend bodies sit inside an
// otherwise against-trend run, so the pullback looks simple on the trading
// timeframe (G01-15, G06-28). Grimes's own reading is lookback 6 with the band
// 4 to 5; those values live in the catalog row and the grid, NOT in the
// defaults.
//
// A BAND IS NOT THIS RULE NEGATED -- a window with NO bear bodies at all fails
// the band and passes the negation -- which is the PullbackNearMissesEntryPrice
// / ShallowDipBelowPriorBarLow precedent and merge decision 19: both bounds on
// one quantity are a new input on the rule that computes the quantity, never a
// second file.
//
// minOpposite DEFAULTS TO 0, which is inert: a CountIF result is never
// negative, so every existing placement and template is unchanged.
//
// RECORDED LOSS: the count does not require the with-trend bars to be
// contiguous or central.
